  盲人导盲犬 | guide dog for the blind
  盲人阅读器 | Braille reader for the blind

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  盲人摸象 | máng rén mō xiàng | blind men groping an elephant; take a part for the whole
  盲人瞎马 | máng rén xiā mǎ | a blind man on a blind horse; rushing headlong into grave danger
  盲目跟从 | máng mù gēn cóng | follow blindly without discernment
  目盲心明 | mù máng xīn míng | blind of eye but clear of heart; intuitive wisdom

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  盲 | máng | blind; sightless; lack vision | ciego; invidente; sin visión | 目 | eye | 目 (eye, organ of vision) | 亡 (wáng, perish / phonetic) | 8 | 上下结构 | Phono-semantic compound: 亡 (loss, destruction) sitting atop 目 (eye), signifying that sight in the eyes has been extinguished. | When sight perishes (亡) from above the physical eye (目), total darkness renders one blind (盲). | Cuando la luz fenece y muere (亡) sobre el órgano del ojo (目), la mirada queda a oscuras, creando la ceguera (盲). | 35 | YVBU | 
  人 | rén | person; human being; someone | persona; ser humano; individuo | 人 | human / person | 人 (biped human figure) | "" | 2 | 单一结构 | Pictogram depicting a human standing upright on two legs, representing moral agency and social humanity. | Two stable strokes leaning together like a human walking upright on the fertile soil of the earth (人). | Dos trazos que se apoyan mutuamente evocando la silueta erguida de un ser humano en camino (人). | 35 | O | 

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: A person (人) whose eyes have lost vision (盲) experiences the physical world through touch and sound as a blind person (盲人).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Una persona (人) cuyos ojos han perdido la visión (盲) percibe el entorno a través del tacto y el oído como invidente (盲人).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In classical Chinese epistemology, 盲 denotes optical sightlessness, but is frequently expanded into philosophical metaphors for cognitive bias (盲目, 盲从). The famous fable of 盲人摸象 from Buddhist sutras (涅槃经) established 盲人 as the archetypal symbol of epistemological limitation.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Dual rising 2nd tones: 'máng rén' (35-35). Ensure smooth melodious elevation on both syllables without dropping tone mid-way.

