semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 盲人 is the standard, respectful noun for a person with visual impairment, used neutrally in both social and allegorical contexts.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 盲人 vs. 瞎子 | xiāzi | 盲人 is the formal, respectful, and standard societal term used in education, law, and literature, whereas 瞎子 is colloquial and can easily sound blunt, abrasive, or derogatory if misused.
    2 | 盲人 vs. 视障者 | shìzhàngzhě | 盲人 primarily denotes individuals with total or near-total blindness, whereas 视障者 (visually impaired persons) is a modern clinical umbrella term including low-vision and partial visual impairments.
    3 | 盲人 vs. 残疾人 | cánjírén | 盲人 specifies visual disability exclusively, whereas 残疾人 is the broad generic term encompassing all physical, sensory, and intellectual disabilities.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 盲人的世界虽然没有斑斓的色彩，但他们的指尖却能触摸到常人难以察觉的细腻肌理。用耳朵倾听风声，用内心体察人情，失明并没有遮蔽他们对生活的热爱，反而让灵魂沉淀得更为纯粹澄澈。 | Mángrén de shìjiè suīrán méiyǒu bānlán de sècǎi, dàn tāmen de zhǐjiān què néng chùmō dào chángrén nányǐ chájào de xìnì jīlǐ. Yòng ěrduo qīngtīng fēngshēng, yòng nèixīn tǐchá rénqíng, shīmíng bìng méiyǒu zhēbì tāmen duì shēnghuó de rè'ài, fǎn'ér ràng línghún chéndiàn de gèngwéi chúncuì chéngchè. | Although the world of blind people lacks resplendent colors, their fingertips can perceive delicate textures imperceptible to others. Listening to winds and intuiting human warmth, blindness never dims their love of life; rather, it distills their souls into pure lucidity. | Aunque el mundo de los invidentes carezca de colores vivos, la yema de sus dedos capta texturas sutiles inadvertidas para la vista. Al escuchar el viento y auscultar el sentir ajeno, la ceguera no apaga su amor por la existencia, sino que dota a su espíritu de serena transparencia.
  #2 | 在无障碍智慧城市建设中，保障盲人群体的出行与数字权益已成为文明发展的重要指标。通过引入高精度语音导航系统与智能触觉感知设备，现代科技正在打破感官隔阂，协助视障人士更加自信从容地融入社会生活。 | Zài wúzhàng'ài zhìhuì chéngshì jiànshè zhōng, bǎozhàng mángrén qúntǐ de chūxíng yǔ shùzì quányì yǐ chéngwéi wénmíng fāzhǎn de zhòngyào zhǐbiāo. Tōngguò yǐnrù gāojīngdù yǔyīn dǎoháng xìtǒng yǔ zhìnéng chùjué gǎnzhī shèbèi, xiàndài kējì zhèngzài dǎpò gǎnguān géhé, xiézhù shìzhàng rénshì gèngjiā zìxìn cóngróng de róngrù shèhuì shēnghuó. | In building barrier-free smart cities, safeguarding the mobility and digital rights of the blind has become a vital benchmark of progress. By introducing precision voice navigation and tactile sensory devices, technology bridges sensory divides, empowering blind citizens to integrate into society. | En el desarrollo de urbes inteligentes e inclusivas, velar por la movilidad y los derechos digitales de los invidentes es signo de madurez social. La navegación por voz y los sensores hápticos derriban barreras sensoriales, permitiendo a las personas con ceguera desenvolverse con plena autonomía.
